Package: linux-icloud-photos
Version: @VERSION@
Section: graphics
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Jaro <jaro@localhost>
Homepage: https://github.com/jgu-linux-apps/linux-icloud-photos
Replaces: icloud-photos-linux
Conflicts: icloud-photos-linux
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), python3-venv, python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-4.0 (>= 4.10), gir1.2-adw-1 (>= 1.2)
Recommends: libgtk-4-media-gstreamer, gstreamer1.0-plugins-good, gstreamer1.0-plugins-bad, gstreamer1.0-libav, heif-gdk-pixbuf, librsvg2-common, mpv, python3-keyring
Description: Unofficial iCloud Photos client for Ubuntu (GTK4)
 Browse iCloud photos, albums, Live Photos and videos by streaming them, without
 syncing the library to disk. Only a small, size-limited thumbnail cache is kept.
 .
 Features: newest-first infinite scroll, zoom, photo information, slideshows,
 upload with album choice, and casting to DLNA/UPnP, Chromecast and AirPlay
 (Apple TV) receivers. Advanced Data Protection must be turned off. The
 unofficial pyicloud library is installed into /opt/linux-icloud-photos/venv.
 .
 Free of charge, may be redistributed unmodified; modification is not permitted
 (see the license). Created with the help of Claude.
